messages:
zoe (DevEx): quick heads-up from support: new user hit broken quickstart, stack trace points to README code block. filing here so we fix before more tickets.
matt (SDK): oh no. what does the README show?
zoe (DevEx): it has this JS example:
```js
const Redwood = require('redwood-js-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
const r = await client.generate('Hello world');
console.log(r.text);
```
zoe (DevEx): runtime: TypeError: client.generate is not a function. also onboarding quickstart lists REDACTED_API_KEY in env examples which users sometimes copy into deploy.
matt (SDK): that explains it. v0.9 renamed package to @redwood/inference-js and split surfaces; method is now client.chat.create (or chat.generate). also default retry changed to 0 (docs still show 3).
hana (docs): i'll open a tiny PR to update the quickstart with a before/after snippet, call out the env var rename to RW_API_KEY, and remove placeholder keys. proposed after snippet: 
```js
// after (working)
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/inference-js');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY, retry: { maxRetries: 2 } });
const resp = await client.chat.create({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello world' }] });
console.log(resp.choices[0].message.content);
```
hana (docs): i'll also add a short migration note at the top of quickstart and a CI smoke step to run node examples.
ci-bot: PR opened by hana: "docs: fix quickstart snippets + migration note" -> https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/932
ci-bot: running examples-smoke (node) for branch docs/fix-quickstart.
ci-bot: examples-smoke failed (run 11): detected placeholder value 'REDACTED_API_KEY' in README -> blocking merge.
hana (docs): replaced placeholders with explicit instruction: export RW_API_KEY=your_real_key and added regex check for placeholders in GH actions. pushed fix.
ci-bot: examples-smoke passed (run 12). node quickstart executed against staging fixture.
matt (SDK): i'll add a small runtime shim that detects legacy env var names (REDWOOD_KEY, OLD_API_KEY) and emits a friendly error pointing to RW_API_KEY. will follow up with a patch.
hana (docs): PR merged and backported to release/v0.9.x. closing loop. tiny snippet drift but big DX impact, thanks for the quick turnaround. :tada:
